{
  "_comment": [
    "Default bindings for the two ports this package declares. The frontend ships no bindings of its",
    "own: a package that declares a controller says how it is played by default, and the user's own",
    "bindings always win.",
    "",
    "The face buttons follow the pad's own geometry rather than a keyboard's alphabet: Cross is the",
    "bottom one and takes the key under the hand, Circle the right, Square the left, Triangle the top.",
    "Analog is a real button on a DualShock - it switches the pad between digital and analog mode,",
    "which a game can see - so it is bound rather than assumed.",
    "",
    "Player 1 keeps the keyboard as well as the first pad; player 2 gets a pad and no keys."
  ],
